<title>INDIA: POLL-India BHEL 1st half net seen higher.</title>
<headline>POLL-India BHEL 1st half net seen higher.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-run Bharat Heavy Electricals Ltd (BHEL) is projected to post 52 percent higher net profit in the first half of fiscal 1997/98 (April-March), a consensus of 18 top brokerages polled by Reuters showed on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Sales are forecast to rise 11.1 percent to 22.7 billion rupees.</p>
<p>Following are the details of the poll compared with actuals for the first half of 1996/97.</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>				NET PROFIT		   SALES</p>
<p>				   (first half to September 30)</p>
<p>			    97/98     96/97	97/98	96/97</p>
<p>					 (in millions of rupees)</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>BHEL    ----PAT seen up 52.0%, sales up 11.1%</p>
<p>Average		1,044.75    687.20    22,684.67  20,408.70</p>
<p>High		   1,960.00		  30,753.50</p>
<p>Low			630.00		  16,327.00</p>
<p>--Bombay equities desk +91-22-265-9000</p>
